This PR fixes critical CSS styling issues that occurred after upgrading to Tailwind CSS v4. The upgrade initially broke the page styling due to utility class incompatibilities between v3 and v4.

## 🐛 Issue

After upgrading to Tailwind CSS v4, the CSS was not displaying correctly on the page. The build was failing with errors about unknown utility classes that were valid in v3 but don't exist in v4.

## 🔧 Root Cause

Tailwind CSS v4 changed how utility classes are generated from CSS custom properties. The following utility classes were no longer recognized:

- `border-border` 
- `bg-background`
- `text-foreground`

Additionally, v4 requires different PostCSS configuration and CSS import syntax.

## ✅ Solution

**Fixed Utility Classes**: Replaced problematic `@apply` directives with direct CSS custom property references:

```css
/* Before (v3 style) */
@apply border-border bg-background text-foreground;

/* After (v4 compatible) */
border-color: hsl(var(--border));
background-color: hsl(var(--background)); 
color: hsl(var(--foreground));
```

**Updated CSS Import**: Changed from v3 directives to v4 syntax:

```css
/* Before */
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components; 
@tailwind utilities;

/* After */
@import "tailwindcss";
```

**PostCSS Configuration**: Ensured correct use of `@tailwindcss/postcss` plugin for v4 compatibility.

## 🎯 Result

- ✅ Build completes successfully with no CSS-related errors
- ✅ All Tailwind CSS styling now displays correctly on the page
- ✅ Maintains all existing visual design and functionality
- ✅ Full compatibility with Tailwind CSS v4 architecture

The application now properly renders with all CSS styling intact while leveraging the improved performance and features of Tailwind CSS v4.

